      formula: "Concept: indirect rule was a low-cost and low-resistance method of control through indigenous rulers.",
      substitution: "Using existing African rulers saved money, avoided the cost of a large European administration and reduced the chance of revolt.",
      calculation: "Because cost and resistance were both lowered, the system appeared efficient to the British, even though it aggravated ethnic differences.",
